{"name":"Goulash","hex":"#8d6449","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goulash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stew of beef or veal and vegetables, flavoured with paprika.","Synonym of American chop suey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goulash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goulash","blocks":[{"text":"Goulash is a meal made of meat and vegetables seasoned with paprika and other spices. Originating in Hungary, goulash is a common meal predominantly eaten in Central Europe but also in other parts of Europe. It is one of the national dishes of Hungary and a symbol of the country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Gulyas080.jpg/330px-Gulyas080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goulash","wikidata":"Q205762"},{"title":"Goulash (bridge)","blocks":[{"text":"Goulash is a style of playing the card game of bridge, normally in friendly play such as rubber bridge, in which the cards are not thoroughly shuffled between consecutive deals. The aim is to create deals where the suits are more unevenly distributed between the players, thus creating \"wild\" deals in order to make the game more vivid."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goulash_(bridge)","wikidata":"Q2925163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jpg/500px-2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jpg/1280px-2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jpg/500px-2009-09-gulasch-p%C3%B6rk%C3%B6lt-paprikas-2.jp